From 10e34090fa3f0a61f2366ce518955d3b9e168f03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zoa Hickenlooper <legitnull0@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:21:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] [client] Ensure onDisconnected is called on connection
 teardown (#8178)

Conn.Close previously called onDisconnected only when evalStatus
reported StatusConnected. When a connection drops or closes from
a connecting or disconnecting state, the callback was skipped.
This left registered listeners such as Rosenpass unaware of the
teardown, keeping peer workers active and leaking sockets.

Invoke onDisconnected unconditionally on Conn.Close if registered.
