From 023b9d4139c1c2c42bceb262adfc54bd4efbeaa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riccardom <riccardomanfrin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:42:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] [client] Keep allowed IPs when only the chosen routing
 peer's status changes

recalculateRoutes did not tell a status change of the chosen routing peer
(idle to connected when traffic wakes it, connected to relayed and back) from
a switch to another peer: it removed the allowed IPs and added them back on
the same peer. In between the prefix had no owner and packets for it were
dropped, and default routes published a spurious "disconnected due to high
availability change" event followed by two "connected" ones.

When the same route stays on the same peer with the same definition, only
the recorded status is updated now.
