From c4d10816f247d64ce6baf4f7c344c46cad68e1cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riccardom <riccardomanfrin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:26:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] [client] Limit the "never" relayed switch policy to
 peers that dropped from direct

NB_HA_RELAYED_SWITCH_DELAY=never keeps a routing peer whose direct
connection dropped to relay for as long as it stays connected. Once the
relayed delay also covered peers that were never direct, "never" pinned
those to the relay for good, although a direct equivalent was available
and the peer showed no sign of turning direct.

A peer that was never direct now uses the default delay under "never",
which keeps the policy's original scope.
