A peer update can recreate a routing peer: modifyPeers removes it from the
interface, which drops its routed prefixes, and adds it back idle with its
overlay addresses only. The remove and re-add that recalculateRoutes used
to run on every status change of the chosen peer put the prefixes back as
a side effect once the peer connected. Without it, a watcher that sees the
same peer go idle and then connected leaves the routed subnet without an
owner until a route update or an HA switch.

