A latency-only switch waited for a sample on both peers. If the current
peer never got one, because its candidate pair stats kept failing or
reporting no round trip time, it kept the route indefinitely against a
measured peer, however much faster that one was.

The hold on an unsampled current peer now lasts unmeasuredLatencyHold
(30s), long enough for a recovered direct connection to report its first
sample. After that the peer is ranked at unknownLatency again and the usual
switch margins apply. relayedHold is armed so the switch is reconsidered
when the hold runs out.
