For a routing peer that was never direct, the relayed delay runs from the
first evaluation that finds a direct contender. It was only reset when the
current peer changed or turned direct, so if that contender went away and
another one showed up later, the delay counted from the first one and the
new contender took over at once.

The delay of such a peer now restarts once no direct contender is left.
The delay of a peer that dropped from direct keeps running from the drop.
